.th SLOGO I Feb/76
.sh NAME
slogo \*- simulation language based on logo
.sh SYNOPSIS
slogo
.br
nglogo
.sh DESCRIPTION
Slogo is a conversational process-oriented discrete stochastic simulation
language with integrated animation facilities.
It is intended to provide an elegant natural means for the expression of
and interaction with a wide range of types of models.
It has been used to model computer system components, transportation systems,
jobshop situations and as a tool for programme animation.
There are currently two versions maintained.
The slogo command supports the full language in all its glory.
Nglogo supports everything but the animation and graphics commands.
They are not completely compatible, since in nglogo it is possible
to define functions whose names conflict with those of graphics commands.
The only reason for using nglogo is that it is slightly smaller,
and so spends marginally less time swapped out,
and it doesn't occupy any double-port memory, so other people can run graphics
sometimes.
A somewhat incomplete version of the Slogo user's manual
is available by typing
     nroff /mnt/td/slogo/man.d
